    "https://jobs.ewu.edu/jobs/nursing-adjunct-professor-part-time-spokane-washington-united-states": {
      "title": "Nursing Adjunct Professor - Part-Time",
      "description": "Nursing Adjunct Professor - Part-Time - Spokane, Washington, United States Nursing Adjunct Professor - Part-Time - Spokane, Washington, United States Kiosk mode CAREERS AT EASTERN Nursing Adjunct Professor - Part-Time 492333 Spokane, Washington College of Health Sciences Adjunct Add to favorites View favorites Applications are currently being accepted for adjunct (part-time) Nursing faculty on a continuous basis. All faculty are expected to engage in effective teaching and assessment of student learning. During the application process you will let us know your preferred teaching disciplines and methods. Demonstrated expertise is required for teaching in the discipline associated with appointment as an adjunct faculty member; expertise is normally demonstrated by one or more of the following: Master’s degree in nursing or Bachelor’s degree in nursing with Master’s degree in a health or education related field Unencumbered Washington Registered Nurse license, or eligible for licensure Current healthcare provider CPR certification Excellent interpersonal communication skills Demonstrated ability to apply a responsive and flexible approach that is supportive to the needs including universal access of our students, faculty staff and the public. Back to job search Equal Opportunity Employer Eastern Washington University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. We recognize that our success is dependent on how well we value, engage, include, and utilize the rich diversity of our faculty, staff, students, and alumni. We believe that prejudice, oppression, and discrimination are detrimental to human development, and that a vibrant and diverse campus community enhances the learning environment of the populations that we serve. We are committed to treating all with dignity and respect, and to working collectively on an ongoing basis to build and maintain a community that understands, celebrates and promotes diversity, while promoting inclusivity at all levels. EWU does not discriminate in its programs and activities on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, genetic information, age, marital status, families with children, protected veteran or military status, HIV or hepatitis C, status as a mother breastfeeding her child, or the presence of any sensory, mental, or physical disability or the use of a trained guide dog or service animal by a person with a disability, as provided for and to the extent required by state and federal laws. Office of Equal Opportunity Join a team dedicated to student success, faculty excellence and community collaboration. At Eastern, our goal is simple: to create an environment where students succeed at their highest level in fulfilling their goals in their education, career and life. Students are at the center of all that Eastern does. For our faculty and staff, this focus means more than just coming to work every day. We strive for excellence in everything we do; we foster a culture of respect, commitment and honesty; and we work to create environments for personal transformation that enrich the lives of individuals, families, communities and our society at large. Working at Eastern also means living and working in a glorious region noted for its affordable housing, good schools, short commutes, over 220 sunny days per year, abundant lakes and mountains, short hops to larger cities (Seattle, Portland, Vancouver), and endless recreation opportunities. For additional information, visit EWU’s website. Annual Security Report Notification The Annual Safety and Fire Report is provided in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Act of 1998 and the associated amendments including the recently adopted Violence Against Women Reauthorization Act of 2013. Per Federal Regulations (34 CFR Part 668), it is required that a copy of Eastern Washington University’s Clery Act Report, otherwise known as the Annual Security and Fire Report, be provided to each employee and student. This report includes statistical information for three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes which occurred on EWU’s campus; certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by EWU and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, EWU’s campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security issues, such as policies and or procedures concerning sexual assault, alcohol use, the Drug-Free Schools Act and other matters. Eastern Washington University Police Department will provide a paper copy of the this report upon request. To request the report call (509) 359-6310. Or click on the following link: Annual Safety Report Additional Information: EWU Campus Map EWU Human Resources EWU Benefits Office City of Cheney West Plains Chamber of Commerce Spokane Chamber of Commerce Apply Now First Name (required) 51c2c8c8 Last Name (required) 0b7a3d50 Email (required) ae840940 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant - E99875 Cheney, Washington Business & Strategy The Office of the Vice President for Business and Strategy at Eastern Washington University is currently seeking applicants for an Executive Assistant to the Vice President for Business and Strategy and the Chief Financial Officer. The Executive Assistant to the Vice President for Business and Strategy and the Chief Financial Officer provides professional administrative and confidential support to the Vice President and to the Chief Financial Officer and works independently and collaboratively to execute a broad portfolio of administrative functions. In this capacity, the position is responsible for planning, organizing, implementing, coordinating, and managing assigned administrative services for the office, exercising independent judgment, as well as decision-making authority in designated areas. The position requires a high degree of personal initiative, flexibility, and personal judgement in all assignments, along with strong verbal and written communication skills, ability to organize and prioritize tasks to ensure smooth workflow, excellence in work standards and a demonstrated interest in providing strong customer service. The Executive Assistant will also provide periodic support for the Board of Trustees, the division and the campus community. Retention Specialist - E99484 Cheney, Washington Office of Academic Affairs The Program Leading to University Success (PLUS) is currently seeking skilled and team-oriented candidates for the following position: Retention Specialist. The Retention Specialist will oversee the implementation, coordination, and evaluation of PLUS programming (Tutoring, Study Groups, Supplemental Instruction, and/or Academic Coaching) in order to support students at Eastern Washington University on both the Cheney and Spokane campuses. The position will also be responsible for the hiring, supervision, training, and evaluation of student workers, including GSAs. The PLUS Retention Specialist will collaborate with PLUS team to provide support to students by utilizing retention strategies and programs that will help the students persist and graduate and by designing, implementing, and evaluating academic success strategies curriculum for PLUS presentations, workshops, and events provided for faculty and various departments on campus. This position reports to the Director of PLUS, and will provide leadership in growing and implementing an exemplary and comprehensive academic coaching program. Operations Manager - Dental Hygiene (E99984) Spokane, Washington College of Health Sciences Eastern Washington University (EWU) invites applications for an Operations Manager to join the Department of Dental Hygiene in the College of Health Science and Public Health. This position plays a critical leadership role in supporting the daily operations of EWU's nationally recognized Dental Hygiene Program and teaching clinic. The Operations Manager reports to the Chair of the Dental Hygiene Department. This individual is the primary assistant to the Chair and future Dental Therapy Program Director and contact for the program. This is a managerial position with responsibilities for staff supervision, budget and resources management. The Operations Manager exercises independent judgment, discretion, and confidentiality and utilizes delegated authority to make and implement plans, decisions, and commitments in areas related to management policies and department business operations. This position has a comprehensive range of responsibilities, including planning, budget development, clinical billing, personnel, payroll, purchasing, special project support, and other administrative functions. Core Competencies for this position include professionalism, leadership, communication skills, organizational and analytical skills, and professional knowledge about the program. The successful candidate will work on-site and join a collaborative and caring faculty and staff committed to diversity, equity, and inclusion, and to excellence in serving the community. Sign Up For Job Alerts Job Alert 3782691a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Health Sciences College of Health Sciences Locations Spokane, Washington Spokane, Washington First Name (required) 34c6aa87 Last Name (required) 17b34a88 Email (required) c6e811d9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.ewu.edu/jobs/lecturer-occupational-therapy-f99221-spokane-washington-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Occupational Therapy F99221",
      "description": "Lecturer - Occupational Therapy F99221 - Spokane, Washington, United States Lecturer - Occupational Therapy F99221 - Spokane, Washington, United States Kiosk mode CAREERS AT EASTERN Lecturer - Occupational Therapy F99221 492307 Spokane, Washington College of Health Sciences Faculty Add to favorites View favorites Job Title: Lecturer - Occupational Therapy F99221 Location: Spokane Campus - Health Sciences and Catalyst Buildings FLSA Status: Exempt Anticipated Start Date: January 4, 2027 Schedule Type: Regular Work Schedule: Schedule will vary from semester to semester to fulfill the position’s responsibilities. Term of Appointment: 9 Months Job Summary: The College of Health Science & Public Health at Eastern Washington University (EWU) is currently seeking a full-time Lecturer for the Department of Occupational Therapy. We are inviting applications from qualified occupational therapists to serve as a full-time Lecturer. Appointment for this position will begin on January 4, 2027. This position is a standard 9-month faculty appointment; the academic calendar typically runs from mid-August to mid-May. This position is designated as fully in-person and requires onsite presence during regular business operations.The Lecturer faculty reports to the Department of Occupational Therapy (DOT) Chair. The full-time Lecturer position will carry a 100% teaching as outlined in the University Collective Bargaining Agreement. Additionally, all faculty are expected to actively participate in student advising and ongoing assessment of student learning. Lecturers play a key role in delivering high-quality graduate instruction, supporting student success through advising and mentorship, and contributing to ongoing assessment of student learning. The Department of Occupational Therapy offers a competitive graduate program for the Master of Occupational Therapy. The MOT program is conducted in a cohort model with 32 students per cohort. The program is completed in 2.5 years. Students complete all academic work during the first two years followed by two 3-month clinical internships. The Department of Occupational Therapy is located within the College of Health Science and Public Health (CHSPH) on the downtown Spokane campus. As a premier college serving the educational needs of the health care practitioners, CHSPH includes nursing, physical therapy, communication sciences and disorders, public health and health administration, wellness and movement sciences, dental hygiene, and Regional Initiatives in Dental Education (RIDE). EWU is committed to supporting and promoting a workforce that is welcoming to all and encourages applicants of all backgrounds to apply for this position. The expected salary upon hire is $71,793. In addition to salary, the university offers a comprehensive benefits package including health insurance, life and disability insurance and retirement. In addition, EWU offers fringe benefits such as tuition waiver for employees, discounted EWU sports tickets, full access to our campus workout facilities at a minimum fee and free transportation through STA buses. For additional information regarding insurance benefits please see our Benefits page: https://inside.ewu.edu/hr/benefits-briefing/benefits/insurance/ Applications are open and accepted until recruitment closes. Screening of applications will begin on August 15, 2026. A three-day notice will be provided prior to closure of recruitment. All materials will be held in strictest confidence; references will not be contacted until candidates have been notified. Eastern Washington University provides an inclusive, equitable, and transformative learning experience, driving the pursuit of knowledge with affordable academic excellence. About Eastern Washington University: Eastern Washington University, a regional, comprehensive public university with an enrollment of over 10,000 students, is one of six state-funded four-year institutions of higher education in Washington, each governed by its own board of trustees. As the region’s polytechnic, we are recognized for our distinctive approach to hands-on learning that leads to in-demand careers. EWU’s 300-acre main campus is located in Cheney, a community of 12,000 residents 16 miles southwest of Washington’s second largest city, Spokane. Eastern also offers programs in downtown Spokane at the innovative, energy-efficient Catalyst building, the SIERR building which is a hub for research, development and advancement of health sciences. In addition, EWU programs can be found at select locations throughout the state, aligned with the needs of the community. Eastern contributes to the vitality of the region and the state through its wide array of bachelor’s and master’s degrees in over 100 fields of study, as well as applied doctorates in physical therapy and educational leadership, offering accessible pathways to career success and personal development to students of all socioeconomic and cultural backgrounds. Eastern Washington University has been recognized for its commitment to helping undergraduate students learn, grow and succeed by Colleges of Distinction, a nationally trusted resource guide for college-bound students. The honor recognizes Eastern as a ’26 -’27 College of Distinction (CoD), the second consecutive year it has received the national recognition. Tribal Land Acknowledgement: At Eastern Washington University, we are proud to recognize the land of the Spokane Tribe and other tribes that shared the land for fishing and trading. The Spokane Tribe, Coeur d’Alene Tribe, Confederated Tribes of the Colville Reservation, the Kalispel Tribe, and the Nez Perce Tribe are integral to the cultural heritage and traditional ethnological knowledge of the land. Native American heritage is woven into the fabric of our institution, enriching our community through tribal culture, historical teachings, and tribal language, and is embraced daily by students, staff, faculty, and the Eastern Washington community. At EWU, we are committed to reflecting on and acknowledging the historical injustices of genocide and the forced removal of tribal peoples and all our relatives. EWU recognizes and honors tribal sovereignty and government to government relationships with tribes. From here forward, EWU will remain committed to supporting, honoring, and recognizing the Native American community and the dynamic contributions that are shared with our university. Equal Opportunity Statement: EWU does not discriminate in its programs and activities on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, national origin, citizenship or immigration status, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, genetic information, age, marital status, families with children, protected veteran or military status, HIV or hepatitis C, status as a mother breastfeeding her child, or the presence of any sensory, mental, or physical disability or the use of a trained guide dog or service animal by a person with a disability, as provided for and to the extent required by state and federal laws. Conditions of Employment: To be considered eligible for appointment into the position, applicants must be available and able to start in the position no later than January 4, 2027. The selected candidate is expected to be located/based on the Spokane campus. This position, during the course of university employment will be involved in the receipt of, or accountability for, university funds or other items of value, as well as the unsupervised access with the developmentally disabled, vulnerable adults or children under the age of 16. The offer of employment is contingent upon successful completion and passing of a background check prior to beginning employment. All new employees must comply with EWU Immunization Policy 602-02 and provide proof of immunity or vaccination to MMR before beginning work at EWU. Waivers for the immunization requirements are available for medical or sincerely held religious beliefs. After starting employment, employees will complete the required training via Canvas. The Office of Employee Belonging, Development, and Leadership will reach out to you concerning Workplace Belonging training and asynchronous New Employee Orientation. Note: Interviews might be conducted via Zoom (camera must be enabled). If so, candidates must be able to demonstrate competence using Zoom and other technologies. Physical Demands: Contact Human Resources at jobs@ewu.edu to obtain a copy of the Essential Functions Analysis which will describe conditions of employment, such as physical demands. Protective Equipment: University, local, regional and state mandates for public and personal protection should be followed as needed. Required Qualifications: Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD), ppOTD from an ACOTE accredited program or equivalent in the field Minimum of four years of clinical experience across a range of practice areas with specific specialty in pediatrics, physical disabilities, and/or neurorehabilitation Some experience lecturing in an MOT and/or OTA program Experience working effectively with inter-professional teams Licensed as an occupational therapist in the state of Washington Demonstrated ability to apply a responsive and flexible approach that is supportive of the needs including universal access of our students, faculty, staff and the public Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Occupational Therapy, ppOTD or PhD in a closely related field Specialty certification (e.g., Certified Hand Therapist, Assistive Technology Practitioner, Infant Mental Health Certification, AOTA Board Certification) Five or more years of diverse clinical experience (e.g., pediatrics, neurorehabilitation, health and wellness) Graduate-level teaching experience Evidence of scholarly publications in occupational therapy or related fields Demonstrated leadership and participation in professional activities Experience working with or serving rural or underserved populations Work Schedule Type: Regular Work Schedule: Schedule will vary from semester to semester to fulfill the position’s responsibilities. Special Instructions to Applicants: It is strongly recommended that you print a copy of these instructions and the position posting before you begin to complete the online application, as the instructions will not be viewable once you begin the application process. Required documentation includes all of the items listed below: Cover Letter – please describe how you meet each of the required and preferred qualifications (if applicable). Curriculum Vitae – please include a list of references as the last page of your CV, including names, title, organization name, phone numbers, email addresses. Teaching Philosophy – maximum of two pages – include a description of your teaching philosophy and a description of your teaching interests. Application Form - Complete the online application form and respond to the online questions, if applicable Mission Statement Response – EWU’s mission is to provide an inclusive, equitable, and transformative learning experience, driving the pursuit of knowledge with affordable academic excellence. We are committed to serving first-generation, Pell-eligible students. How would you contribute to this mission? Please do not upload resumes that include photos of yourself. All materials will be held in strictest confidence; references will not be contacted until candidates have been notified. Note: Letters of Reference are not required at this time. We reserve the right to request letters of reference at a future date, such as once we have identified interview candidates. Proposed Job Duties & Responsibilities 100% of the time: Teaching and Instruction Teach graduate-level occupational therapy courses aligned with area of expertise and program needs Deliver approximately 28–30 contact hours per academic year (mid-August through mid-May), subject to department needs Meet all scheduled classes and maintain consistent instructional presence Plan, organize, and communicate course expectations, including content, materials, assignments, attendance, and evaluation methods Provide instruction in classroom, lab, and applied learning settings Ensure courses align with DOT expectations and Accreditation Council for Occupational Therapy Education (ACOTE) standards Maintain current and valid licensure, as required by the position, is the responsibility of the employee and shall be done at their own expense. Student Support and Evaluation Advise students on academic requirements and career pathways Mentor student research and scholarly development Evaluate student performance and achievement of learning outcomes Provide timely, respectful feedback and communicate evaluations clearly Assign grades based on objective assessment and submit grades by established deadlines Identify students at risk and collaborate with faculty and the Department Chair/Program Director on remediation plans Guide student reflection to support development of clinical skills, techniques, and professional knowledge Scholarship and Professional Development Engage in scholarly activity leading to publication and potential external funding Participate in university teaching and learning development activities Maintain clinical competence through continuing education Maintain current knowledge of curriculum, student policies, and clinical requirements Maintain clinical expertise in assigned practice areas (e.g., pediatrics, adults, assessments) Service and Professional Engagement Provide service to the department, college, university, and the occupational therapy profession Maintain positive relationships with community and clinical partners Serve as a professional role model within the discipline of occupational therapy Note: The above job description is a general outline of the duties and responsibilities typically associated with this position. Specific tasks and responsibilities may vary based on the needs of the department and institution. Back to job search Equal Opportunity Employer Eastern Washington University is committed to diversity and inclusivity. We recognize that our success is dependent on how well we value, engage, include, and utilize the rich diversity of our faculty, staff, students, and alumni. We believe that prejudice, oppression, and discrimination are detrimental to human development, and that a vibrant and diverse campus community enhances the learning environment of the populations that we serve. We are committed to treating all with dignity and respect, and to working collectively on an ongoing basis to build and maintain a community that understands, celebrates and promotes diversity, while promoting inclusivity at all levels. EWU does not discriminate in its programs and activities on the basis of race, color, creed, religion, national origin, sex, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, genetic information, age, marital status, families with children, protected veteran or military status, HIV or hepatitis C, status as a mother breastfeeding her child, or the presence of any sensory, mental, or physical disability or the use of a trained guide dog or service animal by a person with a disability, as provided for and to the extent required by state and federal laws. Office of Equal Opportunity Join a team dedicated to student success, faculty excellence and community collaboration. At Eastern, our goal is simple: to create an environment where students succeed at their highest level in fulfilling their goals in their education, career and life. Students are at the center of all that Eastern does. For our faculty and staff, this focus means more than just coming to work every day. We strive for excellence in everything we do; we foster a culture of respect, commitment and honesty; and we work to create environments for personal transformation that enrich the lives of individuals, families, communities and our society at large. Working at Eastern also means living and working in a glorious region noted for its affordable housing, good schools, short commutes, over 220 sunny days per year, abundant lakes and mountains, short hops to larger cities (Seattle, Portland, Vancouver), and endless recreation opportunities. For additional information, visit EWU’s website. Annual Security Report Notification The Annual Safety and Fire Report is provided in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Act of 1998 and the associated amendments including the recently adopted Violence Against Women Reauthorization Act of 2013. Per Federal Regulations (34 CFR Part 668), it is required that a copy of Eastern Washington University’s Clery Act Report, otherwise known as the Annual Security and Fire Report, be provided to each employee and student. This report includes statistical information for three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes which occurred on EWU’s campus; certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by EWU and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, EWU’s campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security issues, such as policies and or procedures concerning sexual assault, alcohol use, the Drug-Free Schools Act and other matters. Eastern Washington University Police Department will provide a paper copy of the this report upon request. To request the report call (509) 359-6310. Or click on the following link: Annual Safety Report Additional Information: EWU Campus Map EWU Human Resources EWU Benefits Office City of Cheney West Plains Chamber of Commerce Spokane Chamber of Commerce Apply Now First Name (required) a67c3c5d Last Name (required) eb76321e Email (required) 9bdd7d66 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant - E99875 Cheney, Washington Business & Strategy The Office of the Vice President for Business and Strategy at Eastern Washington University is currently seeking applicants for an Executive Assistant to the Vice President for Business and Strategy and the Chief Financial Officer. The Executive Assistant to the Vice President for Business and Strategy and the Chief Financial Officer provides professional administrative and confidential support to the Vice President and to the Chief Financial Officer and works independently and collaboratively to execute a broad portfolio of administrative functions. In this capacity, the position is responsible for planning, organizing, implementing, coordinating, and managing assigned administrative services for the office, exercising independent judgment, as well as decision-making authority in designated areas. The position requires a high degree of personal initiative, flexibility, and personal judgement in all assignments, along with strong verbal and written communication skills, ability to organize and prioritize tasks to ensure smooth workflow, excellence in work standards and a demonstrated interest in providing strong customer service. The Executive Assistant will also provide periodic support for the Board of Trustees, the division and the campus community. Retention Specialist - E99484 Cheney, Washington Office of Academic Affairs The Program Leading to University Success (PLUS) is currently seeking skilled and team-oriented candidates for the following position: Retention Specialist. The Retention Specialist will oversee the implementation, coordination, and evaluation of PLUS programming (Tutoring, Study Groups, Supplemental Instruction, and/or Academic Coaching) in order to support students at Eastern Washington University on both the Cheney and Spokane campuses. The position will also be responsible for the hiring, supervision, training, and evaluation of student workers, including GSAs. The PLUS Retention Specialist will collaborate with PLUS team to provide support to students by utilizing retention strategies and programs that will help the students persi"
