rogramming (Tutoring, Study Groups, Supplemental Instruction, and/or Academic Coaching) in order to support students at Eastern Washington University on both the Cheney and Spokane campuses. The position will also be responsible for the hiring, supervision, training, and evaluation of student workers, including GSAs. The PLUS Retention Specialist will collaborate with PLUS team to provide support to students by utilizing retention strategies and programs that will help the students persist and graduate and by designing, implementing, and evaluating academic success strategies curriculum for PLUS presentations, workshops, and events provided for faculty and various departments on campus. This position reports to the Director of PLUS, and will provide leadership in growing and implementing an exemplary and comprehensive academic coaching program. Operations Manager - Dental Hygiene (E99984) Spokane, Washington College of Health Sciences Eastern Washington University (EWU) invites applications for an Operations Manager to join the Department of Dental Hygiene in the College of Health Science and Public Health. This position plays a critical leadership role in supporting the daily operations of EWU's nationally recognized Dental Hygiene Program and teaching clinic. The Operations Manager reports to the Chair of the Dental Hygiene Department. This individual is the primary assistant to the Chair and future Dental Therapy Program Director and contact for the program. This is a managerial position with responsibilities for staff supervision, budget and resources management. The Operations Manager exercises independent judgment, discretion, and confidentiality and utilizes delegated authority to make and implement plans, decisions, and commitments in areas related to management policies and department business operations. This position has a comprehensive range of responsibilities, including planning, budget development, clinical billing, personnel, payroll, purchasing, spe