r its affordable housing, good schools, short commutes, over 220 sunny days per year, abundant lakes and mountains, short hops to larger cities (Seattle, Portland, Vancouver), and endless recreation opportunities. For additional information, visit EWU’s website. Annual Security Report Notification The Annual Safety and Fire Report is provided in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Act of 1998 and the associated amendments including the recently adopted Violence Against Women Reauthorization Act of 2013. Per Federal Regulations (34 CFR Part 668), it is required that a copy of Eastern Washington University’s Clery Act Report, otherwise known as the Annual Security and Fire Report, be provided to each employee and student. This report includes statistical information for three previous calendar years concerning reported crimes which occurred on EWU’s campus; certain off-campus buildings or properties owned or controlled by EWU and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, EWU’s campus. The report also includes institutional policies concerning campus security issues, such as policies and or procedures concerning sexual assault, alcohol use, the Drug-Free Schools Act and other matters. Eastern Washington University Police Department will provide a paper copy of the this report upon request. To request the report call (509) 359-6310. Or click on the following link: Annual Safety Report Additional Information: EWU Campus Map EWU Human Resources EWU Benefits Office City of Cheney West Plains Chamber of Commerce Spokane Chamber of Commerce Apply Now First Name (required) ab1663ab Last Name (required) a1620680 Email (required) ac83b769 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Assistant Director - Revenue Generation - E99457 Cheney, Washington President's Office Eastern Washington University is seeking an Assistant Director of Revenue Generation. Reporting to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for External Relations, the Director will support all areas of athletics development which includes Annual Giving, Eagle Athletic Fund (EAF), ticket sales and operations efforts for Eastern Washington University’s Department of Athletics. The Director will collaborate with the major giving and annual fund teams in Eastern Washington University Advancement and work with the Athletics ticketing office towards sales goals. This highly motivated professional will develop annual strategies to drive campaigns to grow both participation and financial support within Eagle Athletic Fund and Athletic Ticket Operations units balancing philanthropic generosity from EWU alumni, donors, and fans with the critical revenue needs associated with annual scholarship and operational funding. The successful candidate will make 50-100 outbound calls per week to solicit giving, ticket sales, and special event sales. Additionally, this position will provide support during Night of Champions, EWU Athletics' annual fundraiser as well as EAF donor hospitality. He or she will develop an annual communication and solicitation calendar in collaboration with his/her university counterparts in annual giving. The position will ensure the gift acknowledgment process is timely, accurate and effective and evaluate/lead any enhancements to processes, objectives, and goals to improve reach and effectiveness. Utilizing industry best practices, the successful candidate will constantly evaluate ways to ensure that EWU Athletics is positioned to provide student-athletes with the necessary resources to compete for championships. Open Rank Assistant or Associate Professor - Nursing - F99165 Spokane, Washington College of Health Sciences The College of Health Science & Public Health at Eastern Washington University is currently seeking tenure-track faculty, open rank ranging from Assistant Professor to Associate Professor for the School of Nursing (SON). Appointment rank will depend on the qualifications of the selected candidate(s). "
